  (gr_text_box
    "NOTES:\n\n1. MATERIAL:\n   FR408 or equivalent\n   Surface finish: ENIG\n   Overall thickness: 62 mils +/-10%\n\n2. Fabricate to IPC-6012 (latest revision), Class 2\n\n3. SOLDER RESIST: Blue LPI applied over bare copper or gold/nickel plating\n\n4. SILKSCREEN: White\n\n5. All vendor markings must be on bottom side of PCB\n\n6. LOT CODE IDENTIFICATION:\n   Supplier must add identifier and lot code date to silkscreen.\n   LOT CODE DATE FORMAT: YYWW (YY = 2-digit year, WW = 2-digit week)\n\n7. Drill sizes are finished size after plating\n\n8. 100% electrical bare board test required for continuity\n\n9. IMPEDANCE CONTROL:\n   See Layer Stackup Table on this drawing and refer to ${PART_NUMBER}-PCBStackup.pdf\n\n10. PANELIZATION:\n   2 pieces per array\n   Tab routing required. Tab locations indicated by ::: (see Dimensions Gerber layer)\n   OUTLINE DIMENSION TOLERANCE: +/-0.127 mm\n   0.25-inch rails on all sides\n\n11. POFV: All 10-mil diameter vias must be filled using non-conductive epoxy and plated over.\n\n12. ROHS: Fabricate to meet EU RoHS directive. Supplier must add lead-free marking in silkscreen.\n\n13. UL: Supplier must add UL certification marking (94V-0) in silkscreen.\n\n14. Remove all non-functional pads from internal layers\n\n15. PCIE fingers must be plated with 30 micro inches of hard gold"
    (start 294.7763 19.68204)
    (end 388.9763 84.55357)
    (margins 0 0 0 0)
    (layer "User.5")
    (uuid "65db8a68-d591-4cae-bfc9-2c4d2b01cd39")
    (effects (font (size 0.9652 0.9652) (thickness 0.127)) (justify left top))
    (border no)
    (stroke (width 0.1) (type default))
    (knockout no))
